      "message": "Unlike the usual optimization where you hoist things to the uniform prep, no. Here, we have CPU code that does (eg) XYZ_to_OKLab to each the color stop. Then we lerp the color stops, and finally run OKLab_to_XYZ in the shader. But the last part of XYZ_to_OKLab (and the corresponding first part of OKLab_to_XYZ) is a matrix multiply, which doesn\u0027t alter the lerp. So we can just cut it out on both ends, and get the same answer.",
